#AUTO 35
#NEEDED 0
# RK817 i2c WRITE round-trip test (issue 114, layer 2).
#
# Now that reads work, this confirms the write path. It writes a
# distinctive byte (0x5A) to the RK817's RTC compensation LSB register
# (reg 0x10) — a plain-binary, no-power-rail register that is safe to
# poke and immediately restore — then reads it back, then writes the
# original value back. The whole sequence (write, read-back, restore)
# lives in the pmic_write_test CALL target in src/019-probe-engine.c,
# because an i2c write is a controller transaction, not a single MMIO
# poke, so it cannot be expressed as a probe-language W.
#
# Non-destructive: the original byte is restored before the probe ends.
# Watch the log for "WRITE PASS" with read-back = 0x5A.

CALL pmic_write_test
